 :gaps
 [{:id :policy-and-decisions :priority :release-blocker
   :node ["types.ts#SessionPermissionOptions" "types.ts#ManagedSettingsPermissions" "types.ts#createAttributedResult"
          "types.ts#approveAll" "session.ts#CopilotSession.permissionModeResult" "nodejs/README.md#Permission Result Kinds"]
   :preview [github.copilot-sdk.native-callbacks/permission-result github.copilot-sdk.session-options/groups]
   :why "Applications cannot impose managed policy or request sandbox/mode before the first tool starts. They cannot tell whether a requested mode was refused, identify a human decision, or return documented session/location/permanent approvals. Never broaden a grant as a substitute."
   :detail "ManagedSettingsPermissions declares deny/ask/allow/limitTo and bypass/assisted settings. Unknown disableBypassPermissionsMode strings are forwarded so newer runtime policies fail closed; an empty limitTo denies all hosts. On resume, omission clears the injected layer. Attributed decisions carry result and decisionContext as siblings on the reply; userFeedback is optional. approveAll rejects managed sessions and abstains when managedApprovalRequired is set. No handler leaves work pending."}
  {:id :pending-work :priority :release-blocker
   :node ["types.ts#ResumeSessionOptions.continuePendingWork" "types.ts#SessionToolOptions.definitions" "types.ts#SessionPermissionOptions.onRequest"]
   :preview [github.copilot-sdk.session-options/resume-params github.copilot-sdk.native-callbacks/invoke-request!]
   :why "Setting continuePendingWork or registering a declaration-only tool can leave a request the application has no way to complete."
   :detail "Expose the ability to find and answer pending tools/permissions (including error vs result and permission decision context), not a general raw-RPC escape hatch. No assumption of callback replay or a new broadcast on resume."}
