  {:id :handshake :authority ["client.ts#CopilotClient.verifyProtocolVersion" "client.ts#clientInfoToWire"]
   :note "JSON-RPC 2.0 is not SDK protocol 4. Preview sends connect {} and rejects mismatch. Node also sends supportedTaskKinds [agent, client, shell]; this is a negotiation difference, not a new public knob. Nonempty clientInfo fields map to editorName/editorVersion/extensionName/extensionVersion; omit empty identity. Do not import Node's old-host ping fallback for a pinned runtime."}
  {:id :shape :authority ["client.ts#CopilotClient.createSessionInternal" "client.ts#CopilotClient.resumeSessionWithInitialization"
                         "client.ts#CopilotClient.updateSessionOptionsForMode" "docs/v2-breaking-changes.md"]
   :note "Only high-level grouped fields are input. Session root model, workingDirectory, systemMessage, clientName, configDirectory, enableConfigDiscovery and diagnostics do not move into arbitrary groups. Omission, false, empty and null differ. defaultProvider null clears, omission on resume preserves. agents.definitions[].tools permits null; optional booleans do not. The private optionsCompatibility.ts normalizeClientOptions/normalizeSessionOptions bridges erased JS shapes; not a Clojure compatibility mandate."}
  {:id :open-defaults :authority ["client.ts#CopilotClient.resolveToolFilterOptions" "client.ts#CopilotClient.configDefaultsForMode"
                                  "client.ts#CopilotClient.getSystemMessageConfigForMode" "client.ts#CopilotClient.updateSessionOptionsForMode"]
   :note "Empty mode needs isolated storage and an explicit availableTools (including []). Remove environment_context unless supplied or replace is explicit. Separate post-open options.update sets skipCustomInstructions, localDiscoveryOnly, coauthorEnabled, manageScheduleEnabled, plugins.installed, includedBuiltinSkills. Only localDiscoveryOnly belongs in both requests; plugins.installed is not a public input. Wait for patch; clean up on failure. Node serializes several empty group objects even without inputs; the preview omits them. Do not assert byte equivalence or blanket semantic equivalence."}
  {:id :open-result :authority ["client.ts#CopilotClient.createSessionInternal" "client.ts#CopilotClient.resumeSessionWithInitialization"]
   :note "Create-only name, cloud, trustWorkingDirectory and refreshCustomInstructions differ from resume-only allowTranscriptRecovery, suppressResumeEvent and continuePendingWork. TranscriptRecovery has plannedBackupPath, invalidLineNumbers and sessionStartMoved. permissionModeResult is absent without a request, otherwise {success,mode}. Keep absence distinct from false. Resume can return a different canonical sessionId."}
  {:id :wire-names :authority ["client.ts#toWireLargeOutput" "client.ts#toWireMcpServers" "client.ts#toWireCustomAgents"
                              "client.ts#CopilotClient.toSessionMetadata" "session.ts#CopilotSession.createSendParams"]
   :note "MCP workingDirectory -> cwd, including agents' nested mcpServers. largeOutput.outputDirectory -> outputDir. Metadata/list filter workingDirectory -> wire cwd (preview :cwd); timestamps -> Instants. Send responseSchema -> responseFormat {type:json_schema,jsonSchema:{name:response,strict:true,schema}}; never add a session default. requestHeaders, env, agent hook payloads, tool schema and metadata retain application keys."}
  {:id :callback-wire :authority ["client.ts#extractTransformCallbacks" "client.ts#extractBearerTokenProviders" "client.ts#CopilotClient.createSessionInternal"]
   :note "Register local functions; only declarations, true/false flags or opaque IDs go on wire. Handlerless tool has hasHandler=false. onEvent is local. MCP uses envValueMode=direct. hasHandlers examines actual hook callbacks. Unrelated reverse requests never share session credentials; secret values cannot enter error diagnostics."}
  {:id :manual-response :authority ["types.ts#ResumeSessionOptions.continuePendingWork" "types.ts#SessionPermissionOptions.onRequest"
                                   "types.ts#SessionToolOptions.definitions" "session.ts#CopilotSession._dispatchEvent"]
   :note "The high-level options explicitly rely on pending RPCs. Use session.tools.listPendingRequests/handlePendingToolCall and session.permissions.pendingRequests/handlePendingPermissionRequest as wire evidence. Restore pending IDs without replaying callbacks; no-result means no reply. A generic low-level wrapper or observer does not prove these four capabilities."}
  {:id :turn :authority ["session.ts#CopilotSession.sendWithCompletion" "session.ts#CopilotSession.sendAndWait"]
   :note "Submission acknowledgment is not completion. Correlate by specific request, drain its completionEventId on success/error, reject aborted/non-root results, local timeout is not abort. No structured success for blank, missing, or tool-request responses. Raw JSON Schema returns an event, not parsed data; Zod's parse overload is language-only."}
